here's an interesting media story  another Fox News reporter has quit so we  had Shepard Smith quitting a few weeks  ago this time it's Catherine Herridge  who certainly much less well-known than  Shep Smith Catherine Herridge known more  for holding up documents in front of the  camera during her reports she has quit  Fox News and what's really funny is that  there are conflicting reports she used  the term facts matter she used it in a  statement that was released by her  outgoing employer Fox News and she used  the term facts matter in a statement by  her new upcoming employer CBS News she's  going from Fox News to CBS News but  what's very interesting is that  depending on which of the two statements  you read the interpretation of facts  matter either can appear to be praised  for Fox News or an attack against Fox  News take a look at the two statements  so the statement released via Fox News  was I have received great personal  satisfaction from mentoring the next  generation of reporters and producers  and sharing my journalistic values that  facts matter and enterprise reporting  will always win the day this one seems  to imply that at Fox News she was able  to share her value that facts matter now  when you look at the CBS News statement  from Catherine Herridge CBS News has  always placed a premium on enterprise  journalism and powerful investigations I  feel privileged to join a team where  facts and storytelling will always  matter which of course the second one's  sort of suggesting that at CBS News  facts always matter but where she's  coming from at Fox News facts did not  always matter which of course we know  now as far as Catherine Harridge is  concerned even if this is her taking a  stand against the propaganda echo  chamber of Fox where facts don't matter  I mean if she's not necessarily saying  it I will and most of you know that  facts do not matter at Fox News I have a  hard time feeling super proud of this  stand that she's taking if it is indeed  what she's doing she's been there for a  very long time nothing has actually  changed now on Fox News where  now it's clearly the right thing to do  if you care about facts to quit but at  some point in the past if you cared  about facts it was okay to be at Fox  News and she's also not a particularly  recognizable face there anyway so I'm  not going to you know make any positive  assessments of what she's doing here but  the interesting story is a broader one  about some of the Fox News departures of  the last couple of years so we had megyn  kelly starting some time back after a  very public sort of dispute with then  candidate Trump we had Shep Smith more  recently and then you know some smaller  contributors like Catherine Herridge who  have just more quietly disappeared from  Fox News but in the end and this is  really the big story Fox is still  crushing the ratings there are some  concerning numbers that I'll tell you  about in a moment but Fox News is still  widely dominating the cable news ratings  now there's an argument to be made that  Fox News is the place for a particular  type of audience and therefore they're  sort of coalescing audiences that on the  other side are kind of split between a  broader variety of news outlets that's  the madeleine mathematical argument but  you can't deny that they're still widely  crushing the ratings the one area where  Fox is not doing so well and this may be  interesting upcoming as we get into the  2020 election adults 25 to 54 are  considered like the important  demographic in the news world sometimes  they're referred to as the demo the  demographic that matters Fox's down five  percent in total primetime viewers this  past October compared to the previous  October of 2018 they're down 13 percent  in total day viewers they are down 25%  in the primetime key demographic that  we're talking about age 25 to 54 and  they are down 27 percent in the total  day demographic of adults 25 to 54 so  Fox is doing well they're beating out  CNN they're beating out MSNBC at all  most if not all times of the day across  the spectrum but they are  having a growing problem with this  important key demographic of adults 25  to 54 now fortunately for them them it  doesn't really matter right they don't  need to be profitable since they have  these rich right-wingers that fund them  and that's going to continue I won't say  in perpetuity because nothing lasts  forever particularly in media but for  the foreseeable future but this also  connects to 2020 and it also connects to  the the growing sort of rift between  Donald Trump and Fox News on the one  hand you have the folks like you know  Sean Hannity and Jeanine Pirro and I  believe Laura Ingraham for the most part  is on the Trump train they are  effectively Trump brown nosers  functioning almost as state media on Fox  News on a daily basis Jeanine Pirro on a  weekly basis I think but then you've got  people like Tucker Carlson who's not  always on the Trump train you have Shep  Smith who certainly wasn't and has now  left and Donald Trump over the last year  or 15 months as we've been talking about  has been more and more frequently  promoting the even crazier alternative  to Fox News Oh a N or oann one American  news network  so this is going to be an interesting  media narrative heading into 2020 now  remember in 2016 really 2015 when fox  news was not behind Donald Trump they  were not behind Trump in a less overtly  problematic way for the right because  there were all sorts of more  establishment Republicans that they  could support or be behind Ted Cruz or  Jeb Bush or whoever until eventually  they got behind Donald Trump as it  became clear he was going to be the  nominee this time there is less sort of  plausible reasoning for Fox News a  right-wing echo chamber not to be behind  Trump because there is at least that's  of yet no serious primary challenger to  Donald Trump and it doesn't appear that  there's going to be one so the  circumstances would be far different if  Fox were not to be wholly behind Trump  as we get into the 2020 election I  expect they will be but I think there  might still be some interesting drama to  be seen let me know what you think about  all of this I'm on Twitter at D Pakman  the show is on twitter at david pakman  show and another reminder twitch  livestreams are back I did one on Sunday  night  there will be one or two more upcoming  this week and you can catch those at  twitch.tv slash David Pakman
 

